    "question_type": "mcq",
    "prompt": "A block of mass m moving with velocity v on a frictionless horizontal surface collides with a heavier block of mass 3m at rest on the surface. If the two blocks stick together after the collision, they move with velocity V₁. If instead the collision is perfectly elastic, the lighter block bounces back in the opposite direction and the heavier block moves with velocity V₂. What is the ratio of V₂/V₁?",
    "explanation": "For the perfectly inelastic collision, V₁ = mv/(m+3m) = v/4. For the elastic collision, momentum and relative speed give V₂ = 2mv/(m+3m) = v/2. Therefore V₂/V₁ = (v/2)/(v/4) = 2.",
